WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:04.980
- [Mark] All right, Steve.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.813
Let's hear bro,

00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:08.010
where'd you grow up, where
are you from originally?

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.584
- [Steve] I originally grew
up in Los Angeles, California.

00:00:11.584 --> 00:00:12.417
- [Mark] And tell me about your family,

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:13.977
you grew up with both your parents?

00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:15.683
- No, I never had a father.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.130
My mother, she was,
she was a good provider

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.530
but she was a lousy protector.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.333
She didn't protect me from
people that would hurt me.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.600
When I was abused throughout the years,

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.593
by my uncle,

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.180
he was a drug addict and alcoholic

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.290
and he would just go crazy on me.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.690
And I was just a little boy.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.083
I still have scars on my legs today,

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.550
from when he used to hit
me with a phone cords

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.603
and extension cords.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.200
My mother, she would keep me
out of school for the week

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.130
because she was afraid

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:58.830
of children's services taking me away.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.790
- [Mark] Cause somebody
would see the scars?

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.360
- Yeah, so she didn't let me go to school

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.990
because I was bleeding all in my head

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.530
and things like that.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.350
And I didn't get it back
then, why she kept me

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.170
out of school, but now
that I'm older, I know why.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.870
Because she was afraid
they would take me away.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:18.053
I wish they would have, because maybe now,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.200
I wouldn't be in this
situation that I'm in now.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.390
I would have made better choices.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.313
Just the same as if my father was around,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.250
maybe somewhere down
the line he could have

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.033
guided me in the right direction.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.213
And instead, I chose the streets.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.283
I never finished high school.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.053
I chose drugs and the
street life over my family.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:57.443
I have children that are grown now.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.083
I've been out of their lives,
I've never been a father.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.840
I don't know how to be a father.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.460
And I sort of blame my father,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.603
but I can't put all the blame on him,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.700
because I'm an adult now
and I know the difference

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.100
between right and wrong but,

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.490
I never had a father.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.990
So I don't know how to be one.

00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:26.871
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:02:26.871 --> 00:02:28.506
- I'm 40 years old.

00:02:28.506 --> 00:02:29.603
- [Mark] And how old are your kids?

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.789
- My daughter, she will be 21 in March

00:02:34.789 --> 00:02:38.920
I have two younger boys who are 13 and 11.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.493
I have a 15 year old son.

00:02:45.359 --> 00:02:47.920
I've never done anything for them.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.360
- [Mark] Do you talk to them?

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.003
- I've talked to my
daughter, here and there,

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.730
but because I was never there for her,

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.003
she's doing her own thing.

00:03:02.086 --> 00:03:03.836
You know, she's into the gang life.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.233
And I blame myself for that.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.469
Because if I would have been there,

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:13.533
maybe I could have stopped
her from joining the gang.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.600
My two youngest boys, I was
in and out of their lives,

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.173
because I chose the streets,
over my family once again.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.560
And their mom couldn't take
it anymore, so she let me go.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.073
And I understand why.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.833
I don't have much family.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.733
I haven't seen my mother since 2011.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.623
I have no idea where she is.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.053
My grandparents don't know
where she is, no one knows.

00:03:54.654 --> 00:03:58.313
Ever since my little sister passed away,

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.203
it's like she forgot about me.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.373
She forgot that she
still has one child left.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.593
- [Mark] How'd you lose your sister?

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.130
- I was told that she
was addicted to pills

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.420
and her whole internal

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.613
organs, everything shut down.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.703
That's the story that was given
to me when I was in prison.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.403
I was such a terrible brother to her.

00:04:38.622 --> 00:04:41.623
And I felt so bad, when she passed away.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.023
I still carry that guilt,
of treating her so bad.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.420
Wishing I could go back
in time and change things

00:04:51.638 --> 00:04:53.273
and be a brother to her.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.151
I tell her all the time how sorry I am,

00:04:58.151 --> 00:05:00.120
(sniffing)

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.720
for not being the big brother
that I should've been.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.410
I couldn't stand my
sister, I don't know why,

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.583
I just couldn't.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.564
I couldn't stand being around her.

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:15.893
And when she passed away,

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.363
I felt so bad.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.260
The last time I saw
her, she came down here,

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.110
and she tried to get me to come home,

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.653
and she cried,

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.163
because I refused to get in the car,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.463
and go home with her.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.393
And that's the last time I saw her.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.133
So that guilt, is always going to be,

00:05:44.835 --> 00:05:46.290
(sighing)

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.090
I'm always going to feel that guilt,

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.760
of not going home with
my sister when she cried,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.940
and she pleaded,

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.140
for me to come home and
get off the streets.

00:06:02.474 --> 00:06:06.420
I don't know.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.743
I need help.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.773
I've been downtown for a long time.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:18.124
And I don't know why I'm still here.

00:06:18.124 --> 00:06:19.674
When I know I don't have to be.

00:06:21.631 --> 00:06:23.881
(sniffing)

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.163
I'd give anything to start all over again.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.700
To make the right decisions.

00:06:34.121 --> 00:06:36.380
I've had people in my life,

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:39.833
that tried to guide me,
to do the right thing,

00:06:41.706 --> 00:06:44.243
but I was already hooked on the streets,

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.843
the excitement, the lifestyle.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.113
But now that I'm 40 years old,

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.173
it's not fun anymore.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.250
It tears you down, it wears you out,

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.123
sleeping on the streets every day.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:08.133
Sleeping in a tent or on a
sidewalk or something like that.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.643
It takes a toll on your body.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.520
The worst thing that happened
to me is when I was bit

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.043
by a brown recluse spider,

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.260
and it nearly took my arm off.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.523
- [Mark] Where'd this happen?

00:07:22.523 --> 00:07:23.483
- This happened,

00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:25.810
- [Mark] Were you living on the street?

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:27.363
- Yeah, down here.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.743
This happened,

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.123
2018.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.510
My arm got really big

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.250
- [Mark] Where were you bit?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.507
- On my elbow and it still hasn't healed.

00:07:42.507 --> 00:07:45.337
- [Mark] Oh, why is your arm all dark?

00:07:45.337 --> 00:07:47.187
Is that from the bite?

00:07:47.187 --> 00:07:50.030
- That's from the skin graph.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.497
- [Mark] Oh a skin graph.

00:07:51.497 --> 00:07:54.360
- Yeah, they took color
off of my leg and I guess

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.920
put it on my arm
- Wow

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:00.270
- Because when they cut off
the flesh it was just pink.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.300
So they did what they could with my leg

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.320
and put it on my arm.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.789
- [Mark] Did you almost loose the arm?

00:08:05.789 --> 00:08:10.601
- Yeah, it goes all the way up to here.

00:08:10.601 --> 00:08:12.268
My whole entire arm.

00:08:13.468 --> 00:08:14.635
- [Mark] Geez.

00:08:15.584 --> 00:08:16.566
- It goes all the way up.

00:08:16.566 --> 00:08:17.940
- [Mark] And that's from the spider bite?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.720
- Yeah, it still hasn't
healed all the way,

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.213
and this is 2018.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.920
But because I'm out here on the streets

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.280
and I'm not taking care of myself,

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:32.173
the way I need to the
process is taking longer.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:37.460
- [Mark] What do you think
would have changed your path

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.460
when you were a kid?

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.323
Having your dad?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.533
- I honestly think so.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.440
I'm not going to say
that I would have made

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.230
the best decisions because he was there,

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.580
but something would have changed.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.020
- [Mark] Having a dad who
was a good role model?

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.069
- Yeah.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:57.963
Yeah.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.573
Yes.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.370
I feel so bad

00:09:05.514 --> 00:09:06.900
because I let myself down.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.910
I left my grandparents down.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:12.010
Anybody that could ever cared about me,

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.113
I disappointed them.

00:09:14.617 --> 00:09:16.563
They always had high hopes for me.

00:09:17.616 --> 00:09:19.016
I was an honor roll student.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.480
I didn't started making bad
grades until junior high school.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.303
Once I started doing drugs and
hanging with the wrong crowd,

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:34.190
I would give anything to go back

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.023
and change that.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:42.313
I started hanging out
with gangs at a young age.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:51.063
Then I became a gang member, at one point.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.502
But as I got older, I got tired of it.

00:09:55.502 --> 00:09:58.000
There's no point in gang banging

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.400
because you're either going to jail,

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.210
or you're gonna die.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:06.703
One of the two, there's no
benefits from gang banging.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:08.913
None whatsoever.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.190
I wanted to be a part of something.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:15.493
I wanted to be in a family.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.420
I feel like I'm out here all by myself now

00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:26.170
because I don't know where my mother is.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:28.653
And my father stays in Denver somewhere.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.993
But he's never wanted to be
a part of my life anyway.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.550
He's involved with all his
other children, but me.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.989
I'm the only boy, he has all girls.

00:10:41.989 --> 00:10:45.190
I'm the only one he
has nothing to do with.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.840
And I don't understand that.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.470
How could you do that to me?

00:10:53.851 --> 00:10:58.337
I tried to be apart of his
life but he didn't want it.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.492
He pushed me away.

00:11:03.492 --> 00:11:06.680
Even my grandmother, his mom

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.583
would get upset

00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:13.000
and talk to him about neglecting
me and things like that.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.193
He would still,

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.523
leave me alone.

00:11:24.504 --> 00:11:26.671
(sighing)

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:31.973
I just wanna start over again.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.423
I'm 40 years old now and I
have nothing to show for it.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:44.390
I've been to four different colleges

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:46.460
and I didn't finish any of them.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.080
Because the streets kept calling me.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.903
I kept going back to the streets,

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.420
thinking I can do both, and I can't.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:58.933
And I see that now.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.063
I'm what you would call
a dysfunctional addict.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:09.680
I can't take care of my business and still

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.043
live that street life.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.002
I'm not,

00:12:16.002 --> 00:12:17.780
(sighing)

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:18.613
I can't do it.

00:12:20.509 --> 00:12:23.410
- [Mark] What drugs do
you use, or have you used?

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.493
- Crack cocaine.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.323
In the past I've used PCP.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.253
Marijuana.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.223
I've tried crystal, but
I don't really like it.

00:12:40.035 --> 00:12:41.353
(sighing)

00:12:41.353 --> 00:12:43.520
I just want to start over.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.090
I want to go back to when
my sister was still alive.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.990
She died when she was only 25

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.853
and I had no idea that she was sick.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.380
So when I heard about
it, when I was in prison

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.500
it destroyed me.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.223
Because all that guilt, just
came down on me at once.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.230
I felt so bad for how I
treated her when we were kids.

00:13:09.607 --> 00:13:12.347
And I tell her how sorry I am all the time

00:13:12.347 --> 00:13:14.732
and tell her how much I love her.

00:13:14.732 --> 00:13:16.982
(sniffing)

00:13:18.528 --> 00:13:21.460
(sighing)

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:22.920
She will be 37

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.513
this August.

00:13:26.489 --> 00:13:28.840
(sniffing)

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.310
And I miss her so much.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.290
I would give anything just to hug her

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.880
and tell her how sorry I am

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.967
(sniffing)

00:13:37.967 --> 00:13:39.633
(sighing)

00:13:39.633 --> 00:13:41.883
(sniffing)

00:13:43.447 --> 00:13:44.990
(sniffing)

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:45.823
Thank you.

00:13:46.909 --> 00:13:48.059
(sighing)

00:13:48.059 --> 00:13:50.642
(nose blowing)

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:52.882
(sniffing)

00:13:52.882 --> 00:13:54.965
(sighing)

00:13:54.965 --> 00:13:57.215
(sniffing)

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:02.483
- [Steve] Downtown has been
the downfall of my existence.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:05.343
Ever since I stepped foot down here,

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:07.893
it's been all bad for me.

00:14:08.935 --> 00:14:10.580
(sniffing)

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.593
I can't, it's hard for me to stay away.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:18.460
I do good for a little while.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:21.518
And somehow I live kind
of back here, anyway.

00:14:21.518 --> 00:14:23.799
(sniffing)

00:14:23.799 --> 00:14:24.720
(sighing)

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.453
And I know my sister is,

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.070
disappointed in me

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.869
because I'm still here.

00:14:31.869 --> 00:14:34.119
(sniffing)

00:14:37.833 --> 00:14:40.200
(sighing)

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.400
I don't know what to do.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:46.780
I'm not into the games anymore,
that's one thing I can say.

00:14:50.485 --> 00:14:52.885
I don't know.

00:14:52.885 --> 00:14:53.718
(sighing)

00:14:53.718 --> 00:14:55.968
(sniffing)

00:14:57.292 --> 00:15:02.292
I just,

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.713
I just want to start over, that's it.

00:15:08.554 --> 00:15:10.877
(sniffing)

00:15:10.877 --> 00:15:13.600
I can't believe I made
it to be 40 years old

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.150
after all the things I've done.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.280
I've done a lot of things in
my life that I'm not proud of.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.999
And majority of it is all drug-related.

00:15:25.999 --> 00:15:28.930
- [Mark] What were you in prison for?

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:31.200
- First time I went to
prison was for a violation,

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.060
and then the second time I went to prison

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.693
was for a strong armed robbery.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.713
It was all behind drugs, everything.

00:15:46.705 --> 00:15:48.010
(sighing)

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.283
I gotta get clean.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.320
I need help.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:58.000
I've been in programs before,
but I never finish them.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.850
I always leave the program

00:16:02.386 --> 00:16:03.436
and things like that.

00:16:07.751 --> 00:16:11.486
But, I'm starting to
think that maybe it's time

00:16:11.486 --> 00:16:12.943
that I go to one and stay.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.863
Nothing can happen, but good,

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:24.673
when you're in a program, I
mean, it's better than this.

00:16:27.958 --> 00:16:30.125
(sighing)

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.383
I've never had a job for
more than six months.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.263
I've never been able to hold a job,

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.720
because I, once again I
thought that I could live

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:47.973
my street life and still
take care of business.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:51.313
It's all a lie, I can't do it.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:57.530
And I've had that mind frame

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:58.710
since I was a teenager

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:00.573
thinking I can do both things.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.023
And as you get older,

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:09.980
people start to care less,

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:11.273
because they see that,

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:16.393
or they feel that, you're
never going to change.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.720
Your such and such years
old and you're still

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.803
doing the same thing.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.823
So if I go to jail, I don't
have any support anymore.

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:33.860
Because the people that
care for me, they're tired.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.943
They're tired.

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.030
They don't trust me anymore,

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.073
and I can't blame anyone but myself.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.423
I caused this to happen.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:51.220
I chose to do the drugs and drink alcohol

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.270
and things like that.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.720
And do the things that
I've done in the past,

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.253
to make people not trust me.

00:18:00.554 --> 00:18:03.221
(horns honking)

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.103
I wanna change.

00:18:08.117 --> 00:18:09.640
(sniffing)

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:13.683
I wanna do something,
to make my kids proud.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.953
And make my sister proud.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:21.170
But most importantly to make myself proud.

00:18:24.949 --> 00:18:28.949
(background voices chattering)

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.223
I gotta start somewhere.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.020
I just don't know where to start.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.800
I've been in jail more times downtown

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.693
than I've ever been in my whole life.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.503
And it's all behind drugs.

00:18:55.501 --> 00:18:57.668
(sighing)

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.363
I don't wanna die down here.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:04.963
I've seen a lot of people die, down here.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.720
Whether they were killed or
they died of natural causes

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.970
because they'd been out
here for a long time.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.050
I don't want to be one of those people,

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.003
but I feel like I'm going to be one.

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:19.560
Because I'm still here.

00:19:32.449 --> 00:19:33.660
(sighing)

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:34.623
Still here.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.473
Well, if this is going
out to social media,

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.973
for those who are really paying attention,

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.633
don't take life for granted.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.663
Cherish every moment that
you have with your family,

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:06.673
your children,

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.612
your mother, your father
your grandparents,

00:20:12.612 --> 00:20:13.445
(sniffing)

00:20:13.445 --> 00:20:14.933
because they can all be gone.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.003
With the snap of a finger.

00:20:23.258 --> 00:20:24.490
I have no more family,

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.573
I don't know where anybody is anymore.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.823
My grandparents are dying.

00:20:35.528 --> 00:20:37.695
(sighing)

00:20:40.734 --> 00:20:44.323
And all they wanted me
to do is to do better.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.433
And I can't even do that before they die.

00:20:51.478 --> 00:20:53.910
(sighing)

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:56.823
So I just, stay away from them.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.140
Cause I'm tired of disappointing them.

00:21:02.941 --> 00:21:04.024
I don't want,

00:21:05.974 --> 00:21:08.475
(sniffing)

00:21:08.475 --> 00:21:10.642
(sighing)

00:21:11.705 --> 00:21:13.955
(sniffing)

00:21:18.716 --> 00:21:19.799
I don't know.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.743
My advice to all the parents out there,

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:33.113
watch your kids, very close.

00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:37.720
Pay attention to their
activities and make sure

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:39.920
they're not hanging
around the wrong people.

00:21:44.498 --> 00:21:48.020
Make sure you're not doing drugs,

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:49.320
or they'll end up like me.

00:21:58.813 --> 00:21:59.646
- [Mark] Alright,

00:21:59.646 --> 00:22:02.779
thank you so much for
talking to me and coming in.

00:22:02.779 --> 00:22:03.749
(sighing)

00:22:03.749 --> 00:22:05.999
(sniffing)

00:22:09.249 --> 00:22:11.416
(sighing)

00:22:12.498 --> 00:22:13.331
- Man,

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:19.700
I don't know what else to say,

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:23.300
I'm just, I get all emotional
once I started talking

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:25.743
about my grandparents and my kids,

00:22:27.531 --> 00:22:30.183
and how I haven't accomplished anything.

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:36.663
The only thing I've accomplished,

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:41.583
was, to create more grief for myself.

00:22:43.797 --> 00:22:46.714
(finders clicking)

00:22:51.694 --> 00:22:53.944
(sniffing)

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:56.773
To all the parents,

00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:01.233
love your kids as hard as you can.

00:23:04.410 --> 00:23:07.093
Be there for them, listen to them.

00:23:11.750 --> 00:23:16.510
Acknowledge them and let them
know that they can always come

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:18.560
to you when they need someone to talk to.

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:22.003
Never pushed them away.

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:26.173
Always lift them up.

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:35.903
That's all I can say.

00:23:37.663 --> 00:23:39.913
(sniffing)

00:23:41.376 --> 00:23:43.320
(sighing)

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:46.630
If any of my family is
out there watching this,

00:23:46.630 --> 00:23:47.843
my children,

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:51.083
anyone, whoever cared about me,

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:54.703
I'm so sorry,

00:23:58.819 --> 00:24:01.270
for not being there.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:06.253
I'm so sorry for the huge
disappointment that I've become.

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:08.883
I'm sorry.

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:11.763
Please forgive me.

00:24:14.620 --> 00:24:16.196
That's all I can say.

00:24:16.196 --> 00:24:18.446
(sniffing)

00:24:22.018 --> 00:24:24.703
(sniffing)

00:24:24.703 --> 00:24:26.365
- [Mark] Okay, thank you.

00:24:26.365 --> 00:24:27.365
- Thank you.

00:24:29.048 --> 00:24:29.881
(sighing)

00:24:29.881 --> 00:24:30.714
Oh man.

00:24:33.393 --> 00:24:34.870
- [Mark] You're a great speaker.

00:24:34.870 --> 00:24:35.703
- Thank you.

00:24:37.215 --> 00:24:38.640
(sighing)

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:41.610
I just get all emotional and
stuff when I talk about...

